---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/lib/seo';
---

<PageLayout
  title="About MorningStacks"
  description="MorningStacks is an independent publication about software that operators and founders actually pay for. Published by Riverra Labs LLP."
  eyebrow="About"
  ogSlug="about"
>
  <p>
    MorningStacks is an independent publication about the software stack that operators and founders actually pay for. SaaS, AI tools, and infrastructure. Editorial first, commerce second.
  </p>

  <h2>Publisher</h2>
  <p>
    The publication is published by Riverra Labs LLP. The public contact for the site is{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <p>
    Four sections: <a href="/productivity/">Productivity</a>, <a href="/ai-tools/">AI Tools</a>,{' '}
    <a href="/marketing/">Marketing</a>, and <a href="/developer-tools/">Developer Tools</a>. The{' '}
    <a href="/archive/">archive</a> lists every published piece.
  </p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>
    Affiliate commissions on some links to vendor sites. Commissions do not set the verdict or the coverage list. We do not sell sponsored posts. The <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> is the full version.
  </p>

  <h2>How we test</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> page is the public standard. If a piece does not meet it, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
